  "title": "capture: Handle empty filters correctly",
  "description": "Don't add an argument for an empty filter.\nThe check for an empty (non-NULL) string is not really necessary\nif -f is the last argument, but would be necessary if performing\na check for more than one interface at a time.\n\nThis change is not needed before 19d655766de45944bb20abeabf19bc6863006709\nbecause before that there's a pass to a QString and then back to a\nconst char* that causes the string to never be null, only empty.",
